    - id: 20
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: 'Sloth is typically associated with people who refuse to work or contribute
          to society.  That is something he plays on, but for the most part this
          association is a ruse.  '
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: Block
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 20
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 24
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 1030.6666
        y: 388.33325
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 24
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "He is more closely connected to the lack of empathy.  When a disaster
          happens - it is our job as people to help one another (as teaches the Holy
          Owl).  Tragically, some would rather ignore or cheer at the death of innocents
          if it means that they face one less problem of their own.  It is the inherent
          selfishness of apathy that this devil truly feeds on. Honing your own sense
          of passion and judgement is the best way to avoid this devil\u2019s grasp.\r\n\r\n"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: Block
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 24
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 8
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 1270.6666
        y: 421.6132
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 25
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: All devils know of their history and Greed is no exception.  All devils
          of sin are bound by the specificity of their contracts with mortals.  This
          means that Greed has to give the other party what they want, but that person
          must uphold their end of the deal as well. A broken contract can have terrible
          consequences for whomever breaks it.
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: Block
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 1
        originDialogueID: 25
        destinationConversationID: 1
        destinationDialogueID: 26
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 1097.6653
        y: 478.24347
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 26
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: What the devil of Greed usually wants is his power restored, slaves
          returned, or an economic opportunity in which he can enrich himself.  Unfortunately,
          the rich talk with this devil a lot, but their souls and stories can tell
          what happens when you deal with him.
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 1
      isRoot: 0
